Slice any thick stalks of the @broccolini{1%bunch} in half lengthways so they cook evenly.

Finely mince the @garlic{2%cloves} (1–2).

Heat olive oil in a large pan over medium-high heat

Add the broccolini and toss to coat in the oil. Let it cook undisturbed for ~{3%minutes} (2–3 min) so it can char and blister.

Once it starts to take on colour, add the garlic and a pinch of salt. Toss continuously until fragrant.

Add the @lemon juice{1%tbsp} (it will sizzle straight away), then deglaze the pan with a splash of water.

Continue cooking until the broccolini is just tender and the liquid has mostly evaporated.

Remove from the heat and toss through @parmesan{}(freshly grated) while still warm.

Finish with extra parmesan, a drizzle of olive oil, and @chilli flakes{} (optional) if you like a bit of heat.
